---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ActionButton from "../components/ActionButton.astro";
import ClosingCta from "../components/ClosingCta.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Software & Licensing Audit — ADDD"
  description="Software cost and licensing review, assessed by ADDD as part of the wider technology strategy and the Technology Blueprint: every seat, renewal date and overlapping subscription set against real usage."
  pageName="Software & Licensing Audit"
>
<main class="page--grid">

  <section class="pg-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pg-hero__grid">
        <div class="pg-hero__col">
          <p class="tagline">Part of the Technology Blueprint</p>
          <h1 class="h1">Software &amp; Licensing Audit</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="pg-hero__col">
          <p class="text-md">A complete account of what your practice pays for and what it actually uses. Every seat, every renewal date, every overlapping subscription&mdash;set against real usage, so renewal conversations start from evidence instead of habit. ADDD assesses software cost and licensing as part of the wider technology strategy, usually within a Technology Blueprint.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <ActionButton href="technology-blueprint.html">Technology Blueprint</ActionButton>
            <a class="btn btn--link" href="#how-it-works">How it works <img class="icon" src="assets/icons/chevron_right.svg" alt=""></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="band band--wide"></div>

  <section class="section" id="who-its-for">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title">
        <p class="text-md">This suits practices where software spend has climbed steadily, nobody can explain exactly why, and a large renewal is close enough to matter.</p>
        <div class="section-title__body">
          <p class="tagline">Fit</p>
          <h2 class="h2" style="max-width:16ch">Who it&rsquo;s for</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--3 grid--mt">
        <article class="tile">
          <h3 class="h4">Practices facing a major renewal</h3>
          <p>A multi-year agreement is up and the only available comparison is last year&rsquo;s invoice. You need a position before the conversation, not after it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="tile">
          <h3 class="h4">Finance and operations without visibility</h3>
          <p>Subscriptions sit across departments, cards and cost centres. Nobody holds a single view of what is paid for, by whom, or whether it is used.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="tile">
          <h3 class="h4">Practices paying for seats nobody uses</h3>
          <p>Headcount changed, projects ended, tools were replaced&mdash;but the licences renewed anyway. The cost is real and rarely visible.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <article class="tile tile--outline">
          <h3 class="h4">If you do not yet know what you run</h3>
          <p>An audit prices the stack. If the stack itself is unclear, map it first&mdash;then the numbers mean something.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--link" href="stack-diagnostic.html">Free Tech Stacks <img class="icon" src="assets/icons/chevron_right.svg" alt=""></a>
        </article>
        <article class="tile tile--outline">
          <h3 class="h4">If cost is a symptom of something larger</h3>
          <p>When spending is only one of several connected problems, the audit becomes one input into a broader strategy.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--link" href="technology-blueprint.html">Technology Blueprint <img class="icon" src="assets/icons/chevron_right.svg" alt=""></a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--light" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title">
        <p class="text-md">Four stages across roughly four weeks. The heaviest lift is gathering records at the start; after that the work sits with us until the readout.</p>
        <div class="section-title__body">
          <p class="tagline">Method</p>
          <h2 class="h2">How it works</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="steps__item">
          <p class="tagline tagline--sm steps__label">Stage one</p>
          <div class="steps__body">
            <h3 class="h4">Collect the records</h3>
            <p>Invoices, licence agreements, admin consoles and expense lines. We build one register of every product, contract term, renewal date and seat count.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="steps__item">
          <p class="tagline tagline--sm steps__label">Stage two</p>
          <div class="steps__body">
            <h3 class="h4">Match seats to use</h3>
            <p>Allocated seats are compared against actual activity. Dormant licences, duplicated products and users holding access they no longer need are identified by name.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="steps__item">
          <p class="tagline tagline--sm steps__label">Stage three</p>
          <div class="steps__body">
            <h3 class="h4">Test the commercial position</h3>
            <p>Pricing, tiers and bundling are checked against how comparable products are sold. This is where consolidation and renegotiation opportunities surface.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="steps__item">
          <p class="tagline tagline--sm steps__label">Stage four</p>
          <div class="steps__body">
            <h3 class="h4">Recommendations and renewal calendar</h3>
            <p>You receive a costed set of recommendations&mdash;what to cut, consolidate, renegotiate or leave alone&mdash;plus a dated renewal calendar so the next cycle is planned rather than reactive.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="actions" style="margin-top:3rem">
        <ActionButton href="contact.html">Enquire about software costs</ActionButton>
        <a class="btn btn--link" href="reports.html">Read the research <img class="icon" src="assets/icons/chevron_right.svg" alt=""></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title">
        <p class="text-md">Software cost is rarely the whole problem. These are the routes practices take to the wider questions.</p>
        <div class="section-title__body">
          <h2 class="h2">Where it leads</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--3 grid--mt">
        <article class="tile">
          <h3 class="h4">Technology Blueprint</h3>
          <p>Take software cost into the full practice-wide technology strategy.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--link" href="technology-blueprint.html">Explore <img class="icon" src="assets/icons/chevron_right.svg" alt=""></a>
        </article>
        <article class="tile">
          <h3 class="h4">Workflow Workshop</h3>
          <p>Find where the time goes, using a real project as the test case.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--link" href="workshops-audits.html">Explore <img class="icon" src="assets/icons/chevron_right.svg" alt=""></a>
        </article>
        <article class="tile">
          <h3 class="h4">ADDDvisory</h3>
          <p>Bring vendor and licensing decisions into a standing monthly conversation.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--link" href="advisory.html">Explore <img class="icon" src="assets/icons/chevron_right.svg" alt=""></a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ClosingCta />

</main>
</BaseLayout>
